---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
  data: catalog.sectors
  size: 1
  alias: sector
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/sectors/{{ sector.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  pageId: "sectors-{{ sector.slug }}"
  title: "{{ sector.name | safe }} — Sector dossier"
  description: "{{ sector.id }} {{ sector.name }}: what the sector includes, where AI and robotics could reduce costs, the guardrails, and the honest evidence status."
---
{#- Re-derived from the export's sectors/food.html so the .u-N classes match this
    export. Every field comes from the repository's own dossier via _data/catalog.js
    and _data/sectorContent.js; a field the dossier lacks renders [CONTENT NEEDED].
    Regenerate with tools/rederive_collections.py. -#}
{% from "partials/content-needed.njk" import block as gap, inline as gapInline %}
{% import "partials/figure.njk" as fig %}
{% set sc = sectorContent[sector.slug] %}
<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Sector head -->
<section class="sector-head" data-screen-label="Sector head">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Uncost</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="/sectors/">Sectors</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <span>{{ sector.name }}</span></div>
  <div class="sector-head-grid">
    <div>
      <h1 class="sector-title">{{ sector.name }}.</h1>
      <p class="sector-sub">{% if sector.includes %}{{ sector.includes }}{% else %}{{ gapInline("sector-includes") }}{% endif %}</p>
      <div class="sector-num"><span class="nb">Sector <b>{{ sector.num }} / 15</b></span> &middot; <span class="nb"><span class="status status--{{ sector.statusClass }}">{{ sector.status }}</span></span> &middot; <span class="nb">Dossier <b>{{ sector.id }}</b></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sector-illus-slot">{% image sector.illustration.src, sector.illustration.alt, "100vw", [320, 640, 960], "lazy", "sector-illus" %}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<nav class="anchor-bar" aria-label="Page sections">
  <a href="#scope">Scope &amp; opportunity <span class="cnt">01</span></a>
  <a href="#evidence">Evidence status <span class="cnt">02</span></a>
{%- if sc and sc.workedExample %}
  <a href="#worked">Worked example <span class="cnt">03</span></a>
{%- endif %}
  <a href="#projects">Related projects <span class="cnt">04</span></a>
  <a href="#sources">Sources <span class="cnt">05</span></a>
</nav>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Scope -->
<section id="scope" class="u-15 block block--ink" data-screen-label="Scope">
  <div class="eyebrow">01 · Scope, opportunity, guardrail</div>
  <h2>Where automation could <span class="u-1">bite</span> — and what stays visible.</h2>
  <div class="scope">
    <div><h3><i></i>What it includes</h3><p>{% if sector.includes %}{{ sector.includes }}{% else %}{{ gapInline("sector-includes") }}{% endif %}</p></div>
    <div><h3><i></i>The opportunity</h3><p>{% if sector.opportunity %}{{ sector.opportunity }}{% else %}{{ gapInline("sector-opportunity") }}{% endif %}</p></div>
    <div><h3><i></i>The guardrail</h3><p>{% if sector.guardrail %}{{ sector.guardrail }}{% else %}{{ gapInline("sector-guardrail") }}{% endif %}</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="u-139">Roadmap status: <b class="u-140">Focus</b> — one of the three first-phase sectors, with Shelter and Energy. Status is sequencing, not importance.</p>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Evidence status -->
<section id="evidence" class="block block--ink" data-screen-label="Evidence status">
  <div class="eyebrow">02 · Evidence status</div>
  <h2>No number ships without a <span class="u-1">receipt</span>.</h2>
  <div class="evd-empty">
    {% if sector.evidence %}<h3>{{ sector.evidence }}</h3>{% else %}{{ gap("sector-evidence") }}{% endif %}
    <p>Reviewed source records come before figures. When the first {{ sector.name }} figures publish, each line will carry: value, unit, region, date observed, a source ID from the public register, a confidence label, and the collection method.</p>
{#- R3 figure slot. Renders the shared figure card for any registered figures
    this sector carries. `figures` is not yet set on any sector, so this is
    template only today — when the first sector figures land, they render in the
    same card as /receipts/, /case/ and the homepage, with no further work. -#}
{% set secFigs = sectorContent[sector.slug].figures if sectorContent[sector.slug] else none %}
{% if secFigs %}
    <div class="cards">
{% for sid in secFigs %}
      {{ fig.card(register.byId[sid]) }}
{% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
    <div class="u-141">
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--confirmed">Confirmed</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--estimate">Estimate</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--scenario">Scenario</span>
      <span class="rcpt-conf rcpt-conf--needs-refresh">Needs refresh</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="u-142 rcpt-row"><span class="u-143 rcpt-src"><b class="u-143">Register</b>sources/register.csv — public on GitHub</span><span class="rcpt-updated">Checked July 19, 2026</span></div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Worked example -->
{%- set wx = sc.workedExample if sc else none %}
{%- if wx %}
<section id="worked" class="block" data-screen-label="Worked example">
{%- if wx.measurement %}
  <div class="eyebrow">03 · Where the method stops</div>
  <h2>How far the method goes in {{ sector.name }} — and where it stops.</h2>
{%- else %}
  <div class="eyebrow">03 · How {{ sector.name | lower }} gets uncosted</div>
{#- V19: the scenario phrase — the words after "A worked example:" — takes
    the accent; the full stop stays outside it. A heading with no colon renders
    whole, unaccented. -#}
{%- set sp = wx.scenario.split(": ") %}
{%- set phrase = sp.slice(1).join(": ") %}
{%- set stop = "." if phrase.endsWith(".") else "" %}
  <h2>{% if phrase %}{{ sp[0] }}: <span class="u-1">{{ phrase.slice(0, phrase.length - stop.length) }}</span>{{ stop }}{% else %}{{ wx.scenario }}{% endif %}</h2>
{%- endif %}
  <div class="steps6">
{% for step in wx.steps %}
    {% set bits = step.split(" — ") %}
    <div class="step6"><div class="n">{{ loop.index }}</div><div><h3><b>{{ bits[0] }}</b></h3><p>{{ bits | slice(1) | first | join(" — ") if bits.length > 1 else step }}</p></div></div>
{% endfor %}
  </div>
{%- if wx.measurement %}
  <p class="wx-stop"><strong>Then we stop.</strong> Steps 4 to 6 — matching a mechanism, packaging it for others to run, and tracking whether the cost falls — would put a tool between a person and their {{ wx.stopBetween }}. That needs {{ wx.stopReason }} — and none of that exists yet. Until it does, {{ sector.name }} is a measurement sector: we can show what it costs and where the cost sits. We will not package something for a community group to run.</p>
{%- endif %}
</section>
{%- endif %}

<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Guardrail callout -->
<section class="callout" data-screen-label="Guardrail callout">
  <blockquote>&ldquo;{{ sector.guardrail }}&rdquo;</blockquote>
  <div class="attr">&mdash; The {{ sector.name }} guardrail &middot; dossier {{ sector.id }}</div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Related projects -->
<section id="projects" class="u-15 block block--cream2" data-screen-label="Related projects">
  <div class="eyebrow">04 · Related projects</div>
  <h2>Where {{ sector.name }} shows up in The Projects.</h2>
  <table class="lg">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th class="lg-col-id">ID</th>
        <th>Project</th>
        <th class="lg-col-src">Role for {{ sector.name }}</th>
        <th class="lg-col-conf">Status</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for p in sector.relatedProjects %}
      <tr>
        <td class="id">{{ p.id }}</td>
        <td class="claim"><b><a href="/projects/{{ p.slug }}/">{{ p.display }}</a></b> &mdash; {{ p.line }}</td>
        <td class="src">{% if p.layer %}{{ p.layer }}{% else %}{{ p.tag | capitalize }}{% endif %}</td>
        <td><span class="status status--planned">Draft &mdash; not approved for build</span></td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Sources -->
<section id="sources" class="block" data-screen-label="Sources">
  <div class="eyebrow">05 · Sources</div>
  <h2>The register comes before the figures.</h2>
  <p class="u-144">Every source Uncost uses gets a public ID, publisher, date, license, refresh cadence, and region coverage. The {{ sector.name }} dossier draws on the register as reviewed records are added.</p>
  <div class="srcs">
    <div class="srcs-head"><span>ID</span><span>Source</span></div>
    <div class="src"><div class="src-num">SRC-001</div><div class="src-body"><a href="https://github.com/uncost-org/uncost/blob/main/sources/register.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Uncost final external Movement Plan and Roadmap</a><span class="meta">Governance-control source · 2026-07-15 · confidence: confirmed</span></div></div>
    <div class="u-145 src"><div class="src-num">—</div><div class="src-body">Sector-specific source records are added with review. <a href="https://github.com/uncost-org/uncost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Propose a source on GitHub</a><span class="meta">Official statistics first · licenses recorded at intake</span></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Related sectors -->
<section class="block block--cream2" data-screen-label="Related sectors">
  <div class="eyebrow">Related sectors</div>
  <h2>Keep reading.</h2>
  <div class="related">
{% for rel in relatedSectors[sector.slug] %}
    <a href="/sectors/{{ rel.slug }}/"><span class="{{ rel.sq }}"></span> {{ rel.name }}</a>
{% endfor %}
    <a class="{{ relatedSectors._allLink.linkClass }}" href="/sectors/"><span class="{{ relatedSectors._allLink.squareClass }}"></span> All 15 sectors &rarr;</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION: sectors/food.Sector CTA -->
<section class="block block--ink" data-screen-label="Sector CTA">
  <h2 class="u-146">Help build the {{ sector.name | lower }} evidence.<br><span class="u-1">Sources before slogans.</span></h2>
  <p class="u-147">Early useful roles: source and license review, data methodology, sector research, and — as the work grows — a volunteer {{ sector.name }} sector lead.</p>
  <div class="u-148">
    <a href="/join/" class="u-btn u-btn--primary">Take part</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/uncost-org/uncost" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="u-btn u-btn--outline-cream">The public records</a>
  </div>
</section>
